== Respiratory compliance and participants
<respiratory-compliance-and-participants>
Respiratory phase was assigned in the trial schedule under the instructed 4--4--4--4 box-breathing pattern; trials were not gated online by the belt signal. The archived decoder identifies which prerecorded breathing instruction played and can reconstruct final phase labels from trial-order parity. These procedures identify the instructed half-cycle, not the participant's measured inhalation or exhalation. A respiratory belt was part of the acquisition protocol, but the current publication-pool trial table contains protocol phase labels rather than independently belt-verified phases. The available source recordings do not yet support a uniform trial-by-trial respiratory-compliance audit across all four acquisition versions. Phase-related effects must therefore be interpreted as effects of instructed phase under the compliance assumption.

The released roster contains 42 participant records for adults aged 19--37 years, with 41 complete session records and one partial session. Two records have identical behavioural observations with intervention labels reversed; their correct recording-to-person mapping requires source review. Each participant was scheduled for both VR conditions, and 21 completed each condition order. The registration disclosed eight already-collected pilot participants and a stopping target of 30 complete datasets, 15 in each order. The released roster exceeds that target; dates and the reason for continued collection cannot be reconstructed from these public CSVs and require author documentation before submission. A balanced pooled order split does not establish balance within historical acquisition versions. One participant has behavioral PPS measures without the questionnaire battery. The project owner confirmed ethical approval and authorised public release of the deidentified data after removal of names and verification of a separate backup; approval-body details should be supplied by the authors for the final ethics statement.
